# Serra Voss - leader of the Wayfarer party (Act 1 campsite). Reveals the
# ettersnap hunt, gives the main quest and two sidequests.
# Compile with:  scripts\Compile-Dialogue.ps1

dialogue TSC_Dialogue_Serra

# Act 5: taken on the road east and pulled out of a holding camp. Checked
# BEFORE everything else - whatever she was doing before this, she is
# doing this now.
entry rescued if flag(TSC_Act5_Rescued) and not flag(TSC_SerraRescueTalk)
entry rescued_hub if flag(TSC_Act5_Rescued)
# The city farewell: opened from code (QuestPart_TSC_CompanionsSettle) the
# moment both Wayfarers leave the party at the bard's city. Checked FIRST.
entry city_farewell if flag(TSC_CompanionsSettled) and not flag(TSC_FarewellDone)
# Shard epilogue: the first shard is in hand and the company came to see it.
# Works at the crypt (they come down the rope) or wherever they meet next.
entry shard_epilogue if flag(TSC_ShardRushSeen) and not flag(TSC_SerraShardTalk)
# At Harrowfield (second village visit onward, post-rites): the company kept
# its word and camped outside.
entry village_arrived if flag(TSC_CampAtVillage) and not flag(TSC_SerraVillageTalk)
entry village_hub if flag(TSC_CampAtVillage)
entry hub if flag(TSC_MetParty)
# Bran walked himself back to camp (left unrecruited at the ruin); Serra already
# knows he's alive, so no challenge and no "alive?!" relief. Checked BEFORE
# bran_intro so recruiting him afterwards doesn't rewrite how he got here.
entry bran_walked if flag(TSC_BranAtCamp) and not dead(TSC_Npc_Bran)
# Bran is in the party and standing right here: she sees her scout first, you second.
entry bran_intro if in_party(TSC_Npc_Bran) and nearby(TSC_Npc_Bran)

== bran_intro ==
The woman by the firepit is on her feet with the greatbow half-raised before you've cleared the treeline. Then she sees who's walking beside you, and the tension eases.

"*Underhill.*"

She crosses the camp in five strides. What happens next is not a hug (Serra Voss does not hug), but she takes Bran by the gambeson straps and shakes him once, hard.

"Twelve days. *Twelve.*" Then, over her shoulder, to you: "And you'd be the rider the guild finally sent. You pulled my scout out of the pass and walked him home. That buys you the whole story."

* "Then tell it. What's the guild's best company doing hiding in a pass?" -> reveal
* "He walked himself, mostly. I supplied the destination." -> bran_credit

== bran_credit ==
Bran snorts. "Don't listen. I was holed up talking to a wall I'd named Gerald."

Serra's mouth tightens. It might be the closest thing she does to a smile.

"A wall named Gerald. Aye, that's my scout." She jerks her chin at the fire. "Sit, both of you. If the guild's courier is modest *and* useful, this pass may finally owe us something."

* "I'm listening." -> reveal
    do affinity(+5)

== bran_walked ==
The woman by the firepit watches you come with a hunter's patience, and no challenge. By the woodpile, Bran lifts two fingers off his knee in greeting.

"So. The guild's rider." She nods at her scout. "Bran came over the ridgeline ahead of you, wearing your name out. Found in a ruin by the first courier the guild's sent in a year, and the courier rode on instead of collecting the thanks." She moves over on the log. "Sit. Anyone my scout vouches for gets the whole story."

* "I'm listening." -> reveal

== start ==
The woman by the firepit has a hunter's eyes, and she's aimed them at you since you arrived. A greatbow leans against the log beside her.

"Close enough. Name and business."

* "The guild sent me. And I found Bran, alive, in the border ruin." -> relief
    if not dead(TSC_Npc_Bran)
* "The guild sent me. About your scout, Bran... I'm sorry, captain. He's dead." -> bran_dead
    if dead(TSC_Npc_Bran)
* "Serra Voss, I presume. You're eight weeks overdue." -> overdue

== bran_dead ==
The stillness goes total. For three heartbeats, Serra Voss is a statue holding a bow.

"...Where." Not how. *Where.* You tell her, and she looks east toward the border ruin for a long moment, jaw setting once.

"He was the best watch I ever posted. The pass knew it too; it took eight weeks to catch him." She turns back to you, and the captain is back on duty. Whatever else there is will happen later, on her own watch, alone. "You rode through the thing that killed my scout to bring me a straight answer. That buys you the story, courier. All of it."

* "Then tell it." -> reveal
    do affinity(+5)

== relief ==
Her shoulders ease. It's the first honest movement she's made.

"Alive. *Alive.* Twelve days I've had a knot where that scout should be." She recovers the stillness fast, but not fast enough. "Good. That's... good. Then you've earned the explanation the guild's letter didn't have room for."

* "I'm listening." -> reveal

== overdue ==
"Overdue." She says the word like she's testing its edge. "The guild counts weeks. Out here we count raiders dodged and rations remaining. Sit down, courier, and I'll show you what eight weeks buys."

* "The guild doesn't doubt you, captain. It sent one rider, not an auditor." -> overdue_thaw
    check Persuasion 8 -> overdue_thaw | overdue_frost
* "Then show me." -> reveal
* "First: I found Bran. Alive, in the border ruin." -> relief
    if not dead(TSC_Npc_Bran)
* "First, your scout: I found Bran's trail, and then the pass found him. He's dead, captain." -> bran_dead
    if dead(TSC_Npc_Bran)

== overdue_thaw ==
Serra holds your gaze a moment longer. Then her mouth eases, just slightly.

"One rider, not an auditor. Hm. Whoever taught you to talk earned their fee." She moves over on the log, which from Serra Voss is an embrace. "Sit, then. You've a company's worth of news to hear."

* "I'm listening." -> reveal
    do grant_xp(25); affinity(+5)

== overdue_frost ==
"Pretty words. The guild teaches those instead of map-reading now, does it." She turns back to the fire. "Sit down anyway, courier. Frost or no, you've earned the explanation by getting here."

* "Then explain." -> reveal

== reveal ==
"We came into this pass chasing a shard of the shattered crown, the strongest lead the guild's had in a generation. What we found was better and worse: the shard's long gone, but something *fed* where it was lost."

She lets that sit, then continues:

"An ettersnap. They drink the memories of the dead, and the right rites can pour those memories back out. That creature has the shard's trail in its blood: where it was carried, who carried it, maybe where it lies now. We've stalked it for a season. Three days ago we finally cornered it, in a cave in the deep hills."

* "Then let's go get your memory-drinker." -> accept
* "Ettersnaps are a fireside story." -> skeptic

== skeptic ==
Serra doesn't argue. She reaches into her coat and sets something on the log: a tuft of silver-grey quill-fur, faintly luminous, cold to look at.

"Pulled that off a thornbush at the cave mouth."

* "...Point me at the cave." -> accept

== accept ==
Serra unrolls her map, soft with wear and annotated in three hands, and marks the cave.

"The company's spent, courier. Half-starved and out of tricks. Fresh legs and a fresh blade might be exactly what finishes this hunt. Bring the ettersnap back alive. Oswin has the rites, and I have questions for that creature."

She glances up.

"And talk to me before you ride. The pass has... complications you should hear about. Work, if you'll take it."

# Straight into the hub: taking the main quest is the start of the
# conversation with Serra, not the end of it.
* "I'll take the hunt. And I'll hear the rest." -> hub
    do flag(TSC_MetParty); signal(TSC_Act1_Camp, TSC_MetParty); give_quest(TSC_Act1_Ettersnap)

== city_farewell ==
Serra swings down off her horse in the middle of the city street and starts unstrapping her bedroll from the saddle. That is how you find out the decision has already been made.

"This is where we get off, courier." She nods at the rooftops around you. "The song is here, the bard is here, and whatever taught the song to a beggar is under our boots somewhere. Somebody should be standing on top of it who knows how to wait. That's the company's whole trade."

She hands you the lead rope of the pack horse, keeping nothing but her bow.

"You ride better without us counting your rations. Oswin will work the archives here; I'll work everything that isn't archives. When the road brings you back through, you'll find us - and we'll have earned our keep."

* "Keep each other alive, captain." -> farewell_warm
* "This is your hunt too, Serra." -> farewell_hunt

== farewell_warm ==
"That's the plan. It's always the plan." She takes your arm at the wrist, one hard grip, the closest thing to sentiment she carries. "Watch your back trail, courier. You're worth robbing now."

* [Let them go.] -> end
    do flag(TSC_FarewellDone); affinity(+5)

== farewell_hunt ==
"It is. That's why I'm standing where the next piece of it is going to surface." She shoulders the bedroll. "You carry the shard and the roads, we hold the city and the song. That's not leaving the hunt, courier. That's surrounding it."

* [Let them go.] -> end
    do flag(TSC_FarewellDone); affinity(+5)

== shard_epilogue ==
Serra looks you over the way she counts survivors after a fight: hands, eyes, feet, in that order. Then she looks at the bag with the shard in it, and for one breath the captain lets the hunter show through.

"Two months in a pass, a season before that in the archives, and there it is in a courier's saddlebag." She shakes her head once. "The guild is going to build a statue of you if you keep this up."

She jerks her chin toward Oswin.

"Before you count it done: talk to the scholar. News found us on the road, and he's been vibrating ever since. And courier - wherever this goes next, it doesn't go without us. The company rides with you."

* "I'll hear it." -> end
    do flag(TSC_SerraShardTalk); affinity(+5)
* "Let me breathe first, captain." -> end
    do flag(TSC_SerraShardTalk)

== village_arrived ==
The camp sits north of the village square: two bedrolls, a firepit, Serra's greatbow against a log. She watches you cross the field and nods.

"Told you we'd be here." She jerks her chin at the village. "Came in quiet, camped outside the fence. The farmers never moved on us; they lent us a kettle. Progress."

"Oswin's still working through what the rite showed. Talk to him. And whatever you've stirred up here, keep stirring. The shard is close."

* "Good to have you both at my back again." -> village_hub
    do flag(TSC_SerraVillageTalk); affinity(+5)
* "Settle in. I'll keep working the village." -> village_hub
    do flag(TSC_SerraVillageTalk)

== village_hub ==
Serra sits by the camp fire with her map across her knees, remade for this valley: the village, the hills, fresh pins.

"Courier. What do you need?"

* "What do you make of Harrowfield?" -> village_view
    if not flag(TSC_SerraVillageView)
* "Teach me to hunt the way you do, Serra." -> ranger_teaching
    if quest_succeeded(TSC_Side_Raiders) and not flag(TSC_SerraTaught)
* "Tell me about the company, Serra. The people, not the mission." -> company_talk
    if affinity(>=10) and not flag(TSC_SerraCompanyTalk)
* "Remind me of the mission." -> remind_at_village
* "Just checking in." -> end

== village_view ==
"Good fences, bad sightlines. Full larders and no watch posted." She turns a pin between two fingers. "Farmers who feed strangers and an elder who watches like a soldier. Someone in this village keeps a second ledger, courier. I'd bet the bow on it."

* "Noted, captain." -> village_hub
    do flag(TSC_SerraVillageView); grant_xp(10)

== hub ==
Serra looks up from her map, marking your approach: distance first, intent second.

"Courier. The hunt stands. What do you need?"

* "You mentioned complications. Start with the worst of them." -> raiders
    if not flag(TSC_GaveRaiders)
* "Bran mentioned you lost your raven." -> raven
    if flag(TSC_BranStory) and not flag(TSC_GaveDruid)
* "Eight weeks and no word out. How do you reach the guild?" -> raven
    if not flag(TSC_BranStory) and not flag(TSC_GaveDruid)
* "Teach me to hunt the way you do, Serra." -> ranger_teaching
    if quest_succeeded(TSC_Side_Raiders) and not flag(TSC_SerraTaught)
* "Storm's coming off the peaks by tomorrow night. The high route will ice over." -> weather_read
    if not flag(TSC_SerraWeather)
    check Survival 7 -> weather_read | weather_miss
* "Tell me about the company, Serra. The people, not the mission." -> company_talk
    if affinity(>=10) and not flag(TSC_SerraCompanyTalk)
* "About the hunt... the cave's gone from my map. Mark it again." -> remark
    if not quest_active(TSC_Act1_Ettersnap) and not flag(TSC_RitesDone)
* "Remind me of the mission." -> remind
    if not flag(TSC_RitesDone)
* "Remind me of the mission." -> remind_after_rites
    if flag(TSC_RitesDone) and not flag(TSC_CampAtVillage)
* "Remind me of the mission." -> remind_at_village
    if flag(TSC_CampAtVillage)
* "I need supplies." -> supplies
    if not flag(TSC_Serra_Supplies)
* "Just checking in." -> end

== raiders ==
Serra's jaw tightens.

"A raider band works this pass, and has since before we arrived. Every supply run's a gamble; they took two of our caches and half of Oswin's patience. We've played cat and mouse for weeks because the hunt mattered more."

She looks at you squarely.

"You're fresh, armed, and expendable in ways my company isn't. Find their camp and end it. Consider it a personal favor with the guild's coin behind it."

* "Expendable?" -> apologize
* "Consider them ended." -> hub
    do flag(TSC_GaveRaiders); give_quest(TSC_Side_Raiders)
* "I'll think on it." -> hub

== apologize ==

"Sorry, no offense intended. I'm sure you're more than capable. It's just... I don't *know* you."

* "Consider them ended." -> hub
    do flag(TSC_GaveRaiders); give_quest(TSC_Side_Raiders)
* "I'll think on it." -> hub

== raven ==
"We had a raven for that. A hawk had *her*, three weeks back. Since then the guild's had silence and we've had no way to break it. Which is how you ended up riding out here, so perhaps the hawk did us a favor."

She scratches a name in charcoal on a bark strip.

"There's a druid in the hills, Maewyn Ashvale. Keeps ravens. Prickly as a thornhedge, but I'm betting she'll talk to you; she owes me a favor. Ask her to carry word to the guild that we're alive and on the hunt."

* "I'll find her grove." -> hub
    do flag(TSC_GaveDruid); give_quest(TSC_Side_Druid)
* "Maybe later." -> hub

== weather_read ==
Serra glances at the peaks, reads the same signs, and gives you a look she usually reserves for well-fletched arrows.

"...It will, at that. High route ices, low route floods three days after." She adjusts two pins on her map without another word.

* "Just keeping us dry, captain." -> hub
    do flag(TSC_SerraWeather); grant_xp(25); affinity(+5)

== weather_miss ==
Serra follows your gaze to the peaks, then back to you, unimpressed.

"That's woodsmoke off the raiders' ridge, courier, not stormcloud. Stick to riding; the pass and I have an understanding."

* "Noted, captain." -> hub
    do flag(TSC_SerraWeather)

== ranger_teaching ==
Serra studies you for a long moment. It's the same measuring look she gave you at first meeting, but the calculation has changed.

"You ended the raider band my whole company couldn't shake. That buys you the thing I don't sell." She picks up the greatbow. "Walk with me. First lesson: the pass has been talking about you for days, and you haven't heard a word. We'll fix your ears, then your feet, then your draw."

Two days of tracking, stillness, wind-reading, and loosing arrows at distances you'd have called impossible. Serra teaches as she does everything: precisely, without waste.

* [Learn the Ranger's craft] "Understood, captain." -> hub
    if not flag(TSC_SerraTaught)
    do flag(TSC_SerraTaught); learn_class(TSC_Class_Ranger); grant_xp(25); affinity(+5)
* "Another time. The hunt first." -> hub

== company_talk ==
Serra looks at the fire for a while before answering. It is her version of clearing her throat.

"Oswin signed on to read the world's oldest library and got eight weeks of rat stew. Never once asked to turn back. Bran holds any door you put him in front of and calls it a quiet life." She glances up at you. "That's the company."

* "Good to know." -> hub
    do flag(TSC_SerraCompanyTalk); grant_xp(10)

# Safety hatch: the hunt's objective was lost (site vanished in an older
# build, or the quest otherwise died without the rites happening). Serra
# re-marks the cave, which spawns a fresh site and creature.
== remark ==
Serra looks at you as she would at a snapped bowstring: recalculating.

"Lost the *cave*." She unrolls the map without another word and marks it again, pressing hard enough to tear. "The creature hasn't moved; it has outwaited better. Don't make me draw this a third time."

* "Won't happen twice, captain." -> hub
    do give_quest(TSC_Act1_Ettersnap)

== remind ==
"The ettersnap. The cave. Alive." She counts them off on three fingers, then adds a fourth: "And talk to Oswin before you go. He knows what the creature can't resist, and where to find it. His books are insufferable and correct."

* "Understood." -> hub

# Post-rites, still in the pass: the hunt is over and the vision replaced it.
# She points at the village now, not the cave, and promises to follow.
== remind_after_rites ==
"The hunt's done. What the creature gave us is a crypt, a sleeping sanguophage, and a shard of the crown lying next to it." She taps the map twice. "The lake in the vision is an hour east of a village called Harrowfield. That's where you're going. Ask Oswin for the rest; he's been chewing on it since we broke the circle."

She looks up.

"Find someone in that village who knows what's under those hills. Oswin and I will pack the camp and meet you there."

* "Understood." -> hub

# The promise is kept: they are camped outside Harrowfield. No more travel
# plans, just the work in front of her.
== remind_at_village ==
"A crypt in these hills, a sanguophage asleep in it, and a shard of the crown lying next to it. That's what the creature gave us and that's all it gave us." She turns a pin between her fingers without setting it down.

"So we're here, and we're staying until this valley gives up the door. Work the village, courier. Oswin works the books. Somebody in Harrowfield has known where that crypt is their whole life and has good reasons not to say so."

* "Understood." -> village_hub

== supplies ==

"There are some rations in one of the crates in our camp. You're welcome to them. Beyond that, you'll have to fend for yourself. If you passed the guild's training, I know you're capable of doing so."

* "Understood." -> hub
    do flag(TSC_Serra_Supplies)

== rescued ==
She is on her feet before anyone offers a hand, and she does not thank anybody until she has counted heads.

"All still standing. Good." Then, flatly: "You will want to know how a Wayfarer company leader ends up roped in a shed. The answer is eleven of them and a bridge I should not have crossed at dusk. Write it down and learn from it, because I intend to never say it again."

* "Are you hurt?" -> hurt
* "Why were you on this road at all?" -> road
* [Say nothing. She is clearly working up to something.] -> road

== hurt ==
"Nothing that matters." She rolls the shoulder that clearly does matter. "They wanted us sold, not dead. There is a market for people who know where things are buried, and Oswin talks in his sleep."

* "Why were you on this road at all?" -> road

== road ==
"Because you are." She says it without accusation. "The whole east country knows something is moving. Half the roads have gone quiet and the other half are full of men in a hurry, and every one of them is headed the same direction as you."

She looks at the packs. Not the faces. The packs.

"I am not going to ask what you are carrying. I already know, near enough. I have spent a year hearing about a company that keeps walking out of places nobody walks out of, and there is only one thing that would explain the roads emptying like this."

* "Four of five. We are going for the last one." -> told
* "Then you know why we cannot leave you here." -> told

== told ==
"Four." She takes that as she takes weather. "Right."

A long pause, and then the only speech Serra Voss has ever given.

"My company is done - not the ones of us still breathing, the thing itself, the charter with my name under it. It died a year ago in a city street, and I have spent the year since deciding whether that was my fault. Turns out the answer does not matter, because the road is still there and someone still has to walk it." She picks up somebody else's spear off the ground and checks the shaft. "So I am coming. Not for the guild, not for a rate, and not because you saved me, which I will be resenting for approximately one more day."

"Because you are going to need somebody who has done this before, and there is nobody left who has done this except me."

* [Welcome her back.] -> end
    do flag(TSC_SerraRescueTalk); grant_xp(50)

== rescued_hub ==
Serra has her back to a rock and her eyes on the treeline. They have been there since the camp.

"Say it."

* "How are you holding up?" -> hub_holding
* "What do you make of the road ahead?" -> hub_road
* [Leave her to her watch.] -> end

== hub_holding ==
"I am walking, I am armed, and I am not in a shed. Compared to last week this is a holiday."

She does not look away from the trees.

"Ask me again after the barrow."

* [Leave her to her watch.] -> end

== hub_road ==
"Too quiet, and quiet the wrong way. Not empty-quiet. Waiting-quiet." She shifts the spear. "Whatever is at the end of this, it has had eight hundred years to get ready and we have had a fortnight. I do not love the odds."

"But I have taken worse contracts on worse terms, and I am still here. Mostly."

* [Leave her to her watch.] -> end
